DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       iibbvv__ccrreeaattee__qqpp(())  creates  a queue pair (QP) associated with the protec‐
       tion domain _p_d.   The  argument  _q_p___i_n_i_t___a_t_t_r  is  an  ibv_qp_init_attr
       struct, as defined in <infiniband/verbs.h>.

       struct ibv_qp_init_attr {
               void                   *qp_context;     /* Associated context of the QP */
               struct ibv_cq          *send_cq;        /* CQ to be associated with the Send Queue (SQ) */
               struct ibv_cq          *recv_cq;        /* CQ to be associated with the Receive Queue (RQ) */
               struct ibv_srq         *srq;            /* SRQ handle if QP is to be associated with an SRQ, otherwise NULL */
               struct ibv_qp_cap       cap;            /* QP capabilities */
               enum ibv_qp_type        qp_type;        /* QP Transport Service Type: IBV_QPT_RC, IBV_QPT_UC, IBV_QPT_UD or IBV_QPT_RAW_PACKET */
               int                     sq_sig_all;     /* If set, each Work Request (WR) submitted to the SQ generates a completion entry */
       };

       struct ibv_qp_cap {
               uint32_t                max_send_wr;    /* Requested max number of outstanding WRs in the SQ */
               uint32_t                max_recv_wr;    /* Requested max number of outstanding WRs in the RQ */
               uint32_t                max_send_sge;   /* Requested max number of scatter/gather (s/g) elements in a WR in the SQ */
               uint32_t                max_recv_sge;   /* Requested max number of s/g elements in a WR in the SQ */
               uint32_t                max_inline_data;/* Requested max number of data (bytes) that can be posted inline to the SQ, otherwise 0 */
       };

       The  function  iibbvv__ccrreeaattee__qqpp(()) will update the _q_p___i_n_i_t___a_t_t_r->cap struct
       with the actual QP values of the QP that was created; the  values  will
       be greater than or equal to the values requested.

       iibbvv__ddeessttrrooyy__qqpp(()) destroys the QP _q_p.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       iibbvv__ccrreeaattee__qqpp(()) returns a pointer to the created QP, or NULL if the re‐
       quest fails.  Check the QP number (qqpp__nnuumm) in the returned QP.

       iibbvv__ddeessttrrooyy__qqpp(()) returns 0 on success, or the value of errno on failure
       (which indicates the failure reason).

NNOOTTEESS
       iibbvv__ccrreeaattee__qqpp(()) will fail if a it is asked to create QP of a type other
       than IIBBVV__QQPPTT__RRCC or IIBBVV__QQPPTT__UUDD associated with an SRQ.

       The attributes max_recv_wr and max_recv_sge  are  ignored  by  iibbvv__ccrree‐‐
       aattee__qqpp(()) if the QP is to be associated with an SRQ.

       iibbvv__ddeessttrrooyy__qqpp(()) fails if the QP is attached to a multicast group.

